[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-3859"] :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-2x<8.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & <8 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-8 & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-2x-8$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/83e87f616c1e9a74065016df2d6a0bbfac5bcdc8ee9326721b13a2bd8a8f16d4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-8<0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-3952"] :question/problem "Find the solution of $-6{x}^{2}>-3x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2} & >-3x \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+3x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-6{x}^{2}+3x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ -3x(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/3dff64c74abd4981c69686cbbf7d79fdd49c7a7fde3bb266b2b6e11c441bcf20.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-6{x}^{2}+3x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "0fcaa68c-20d1-560a-80a4-8d8d524032ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd4924d-570a-559d-b2dc-f56e552f2ee0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276402/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-276402/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "d393db0e-75b4-5c46-834f-a74cc084b33a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "a01c1233-e863-5907-aa31-4700b542c890" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276402/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-276402/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402/field-3/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "cc99565c-080c-5c9b-96d1-0d0f950e06bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "49191652-8c7a-52ab-9393-0549495c3b5d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276402/field-3/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-276402/field-3/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276402" :question/id #uuid "c0311ef6-fe92-51b8-a43d-3cc837a8ac32" :question/math-academy-id "q-276402" :question/problem "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-8x<0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-8x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =0 \\\\ x(x-8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=8,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/8c4acb1db29c8479f946d6d047fe79d9a87d7162de1ff0725e59052f93df85ce.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0<x<8.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276402/field-1" "q-276402/field-2" "q-276402/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbe80595-c807-506c-a356-566f1edb3402"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276402"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407/selection/a7bb17e2e5592b1b8db3cc4ec7d3bc48132fccb5d8944a72ef8665cf75e96544" :answer/id #uuid "3b55f7bb-d26d-55e3-b17f-7c1623a1c745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407/selection/2908297407de95dc5c1f8505bbee71a16e72b8e496b140a1df60694667b3aba0" :answer/id #uuid "ca4696f2-7f99-5bb5-a2e6-2f896009a3cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{3}{2}]\\cup [1,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407/selection/5a2bc58cfab3973a9e463e20ca04a81d9c0551e5a4117aa6420d3c2c3c97113d" :answer/id #uuid "4fb63f72-c77c-597e-a6e6-7af09edbaf8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407/selection/310d7d036b859ce74fcf784ae2c1cfa7148491bee4041d95e8b754a14620371e" :answer/id #uuid "b39057be-c22a-538e-b6d8-b817efa2b994" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407/selection/e04bde83da68d6bbc73bc52a64dce6c80da9689079e256fb17cd23365f2361a4" :answer/id #uuid "9447c28b-d9a2-5fcb-8884-1bc8b89ca063" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6edfb28-dc7c-5965-a229-4e405703ffe3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-276407/selection/a7bb17e2e5592b1b8db3cc4ec7d3bc48132fccb5d8944a72ef8665cf75e96544" :answer-field/choices ["q-276407/selection/a7bb17e2e5592b1b8db3cc4ec7d3bc48132fccb5d8944a72ef8665cf75e96544" "q-276407/selection/2908297407de95dc5c1f8505bbee71a16e72b8e496b140a1df60694667b3aba0" "q-276407/selection/5a2bc58cfab3973a9e463e20ca04a81d9c0551e5a4117aa6420d3c2c3c97113d" "q-276407/selection/310d7d036b859ce74fcf784ae2c1cfa7148491bee4041d95e8b754a14620371e" "q-276407/selection/e04bde83da68d6bbc73bc52a64dce6c80da9689079e256fb17cd23365f2361a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276407" :question/id #uuid "d17d341f-d303-5767-85ec-0a66ef9ec1ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-276407" :question/problem "Find the solution of $x+3\\ge 2{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & \\ge 2{x}^{2} \\\\ -2{x}^{2}+x+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}+x+3$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}+x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-x-3 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-3x)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ x(2x-3)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)(x-\\frac{3}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/86d7fbea75961bdb83c014ca9febb735e6a1745f71e8e094de416998b2072630.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+x+3\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-276407/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276407"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-276408/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "894b802a-63f9-5a6a-bcd2-d93dcfbcdff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276408/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8572a649-145f-5e57-850c-73e70d41aafb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276408/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-276408/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276408/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "aea1369d-d4c7-5774-96ed-e33aece856fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-276408/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff9e19c9-79f3-5995-9c26-a1b6ff4d3e07" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-276408/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-276408/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-276408" :question/id #uuid "d3f622fb-d8a5-5f8e-a1ab-925800ff1e0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-276408" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}\\le 12x$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & \\le 12x \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-12x & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-12x$ lies **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-12x & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/d81805f304bd45ddd595bd251202226d2b1ced494fe7816d0bc9f17ee8f998a0.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-12x\\le 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,3].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-276408/field-1" "q-276408/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d88d6dd3-9da2-5bad-a373-7c62c3004b8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-276408"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
